# tds-tools — local dev environment
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) before `npm run dev` or `npm run build`.
# Astro inlines anything prefixed with `PUBLIC_` into the client bundle at
# build time. Anything without the prefix stays server-only.
#
# Every default here is the production URL, so an empty `.env` is enough for
# read-only development against live content. Point them at
# `http://localhost:<port>` to work against a local API — `:8080` is the
# gateway in tds-gateway-api's Docker stack, `:8000` the one from
# `composer start`.

# The API origin, NO path. `src/lib/connection.ts` uses it as the fallback for
# the catalog read (`GET /tools/catalog`) and the tool guides
# (`GET /tools/guides`). On a paired host the stored connection wins over it.
# Unset == https://api.tracht-digital.de
PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.tracht-digital.de

# Where the premium/login gate sends a logged-out visitor (ToolGate.tsx).
# Unset == https://auth.tracht-digital.de
PUBLIC_LOGIN_URL=https://auth.tracht-digital.de

# `true` → build with the static fallback catalog and ads off, so the site
# renders with no backend at all. Used by the dev branch.
PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=false

# --- server-only credentials (never PUBLIC_) --------------------------------

# The site key for the catalog + guide reads, issued in the admin panel under
# Einstellungen → Site-Verbindungen and shown there only once.
#
# Set it on the HOST as well, not only in CI: `src/lib/siteKey.ts` reads it at
# module load, which under SSR is server boot, so a key given only to the build
# never reaches a request-time fetch. Harmless while enforcement is `off`/
# `warn`; under `enforce` the reads 401, fail soft, and the site quietly serves
# manifest defaults with ads off.
#
# NOT PUBLIC_-prefixed on purpose: a PUBLIC_ variable is inlined into the
# shipped bundle, which would publish the credential.
TDS_SITE_KEY=

# Token for this site's own cache control plane (`/tds/cache/{status,rebuild,
# purge}`), which the admin panel calls after a catalog or guide change. Must
# match the token entered in the panel. Unset → the control plane answers 503
# and does nothing; the site still works, it just re-renders on every request.
TDS_CACHE_TOKEN=

# --- shell-only (NOT in this file) ------------------------------------------
# NPM_TOKEN authenticates against GitHub Packages for tds-shared and the tool
# packs. npm does not load `.env`:
#   PowerShell:  $env:NPM_TOKEN = "ghp_…"
#   bash/zsh:    export NPM_TOKEN=ghp_…

# --- Two keys that deliberately do NOT exist --------------------------------
# `CATALOG_API_URL` and `TOOLS_REGISTRY_TOKEN` were declared, documented and
# read by nothing: neither carries a PUBLIC_ prefix and there is no envField
# schema, so Vite left both undefined for the platform's whole life and the
# `??` default was the only value either ever had. They are gone. Do not
# reintroduce them — a key with no working reader is worse than a constant,
# because it reads like configuration that exists.

# --- Local note: no pairing over http ---------------------------------------
# The `/install` wizard pairs a DEPLOYED site with the API and stores the
# credentials outside the checkout. It cannot be used on localhost: the
# connection store accepts only `https:` origins when it writes
# (tds-shared/connection), so a local attempt gets as far as saving and then
# fails with `state_write_failed` (500). Locally the variables above ARE the
# connection.
